      "widgets_values": [
        "SWAN STUDIOS - SAME FACE, NEW SCENE  (identity reference - runs on YOUR 5090)\n\nTakes ONE picture of a person and re-renders THAT SAME FACE in any scene\nyou type. This is the dataset-builder for the avatar pipeline: pick your\nhero face once, then generate 25-30 varied shots of her (angles, lighting,\noutfits, places) - and THAT varied set trains the character LoRA.\n\nHOW TO USE\n  1. Node A: upload / pick the hero image (the face to keep).\n  2. Node 5: describe the NEW scene. Start the prompt with\n     'The same woman...' / 'The same man...' - it anchors identity.\n  3. Run. ~30s per image. Output: swan/identity_ref/\n\nPROVEN 2026-09-01: candidate_00010 re-rendered in an alpine meadow at\ngolden hour - same face, same jacket, new world (30.0s, seed 99).\n\nQUIRK TO KNOW: if the output size's aspect differs a lot from the\nreference, the model sometimes composes side-by-side panels. Fix: keep\n1280x704 references with 1280x704 output, or crop the result.\n\nRecipe stays: 8 steps / cfg 1.0 / euler / simple. Seed FIXED - bump it\nyourself per variation so every image is reproducible.\nMechanism: TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus embeds the reference image into\nthe conditioning; ReferenceLatent attaches the reference latent. Core\nComfyUI nodes - no custom nodes, no extra downloads."
      ],
      "title": "Note"
    }
